IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cta-community`

-- Community Titles Act 2018 (WA), ss 16, 17, 47, 48, 70-72, 85, 87, 88, 97, 106, 107, 130-138, 162, 175 and regs 8, 59, 60, 77-79, 84, 173 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. The regulations' numbers are from the deposited Community Titles Regulations 2021.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_community-titles-act-2018_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts from the WA life (workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe). The scenario gives the townhouse, its
-- suburb, its price and the buyers, but no tier, unit entitlements, budgets or lot counts, so every such figure used with
-- it is the encoder's, chosen for arithmetic:
--   chloe c081 (2040): a townhouse in a community titles scheme in Baldivis, $1,300,000, bought with Liam as co-owners,
--     from a private seller; the encoder places it as a tier 2 lot in a 12-lot tier 2 scheme, unit entitlement 80 of
--     1 000, whose tier 2 parcel carries 150 of 1 000 in the tier 1 scheme; tier 2 budget $36 000 a year; tier 1 levy
--     $200 000 a year; arrears interest fixed by the tier 2 corporation at 10% a year.

§ `fixtures`

